      "id": "node-input-prompt",
      "name": "User Request Prompt",
      "kind": "input",
      "status": "success",
      "description": "Original user prompt request initiating the run.",
      "sectionId": "sec-planning",
      "prompt": "You are the Autonomous Run Director for implementing the Capsule Summary Engine in `skills` and the Graph Visualizer Integration in `gvui`.\n\nReference the authoritative specification in `docs/planning/gvui-execution-graph/01-capsule-summary-and-gvui-integration-plan.md`.\n\n### Core Rules & Standards:\n1. Use the GLOBAL harness binary: `PINNED=~/.agents/skills/orchestrating-long-tasks/scripts/harness.ts`\n2. Initialize a dedicated run capsule under `/Users/onurseckinsenoglu/repos/gvui/.capsules/2026-08-14-gvui-integration/` using `plan:init` with verbatim prompt capture.\n3. NEVER read internal TypeScript runtime source files of the harness; treat the CLI as an executable tool.\n4. Strict TypeScript typing: ZERO `any`, `@ts-ignore`, or `@ts-expect-error`.\n5. Modular file size invariants: All production files <= 200 lines; all test files <= 250 lines.\n\n### Implementation Tasks Breakdown:\n\n#### Group A: `skills` Repository (`/Users/onurseckinsenoglu/repos/skills`)\n- **Task `task-summary-types`**: `orchestrating-long-tasks/scripts/src/summary/types.ts` defining data types for timeline events, rollup metrics, command execution details, finding details, and summary options.\n- **Task `task-timeline-collector`**: `orchestrating-long-tasks/scripts/src/summary/timeline-collector.ts` harvesting chronological events from `events.jsonl` across all 18 CLI commands.\n- **Task `task-metrics-collector`**: `orchestrating-long-tasks/scripts/src/summary/metrics-collector.ts` computing wall-clock time, active compute duration, token estimations, repair rates, and diff volume.\n- **Task `task-graph-generator`**: `orchestrating-long-tasks/scripts/src/summary/graph-generator.ts` translating `state.json`, `events.jsonl`, `commands/`, `findings/`, and `reports/` into a GVUI-compliant `GraphDataset` (nodes, edges, loopback repair edges, sections, and metadata).\n- **Task `task-markdown-formatter`**: `orchestrating-long-tasks/scripts/src/summary/markdown-formatter.ts` generating the human-readable executive brief `summary.md`.\n- **Task `task-summary-core`**: `orchestrating-long-tasks/scripts/src/summary/generate-summary.ts` orchestrating the synthesis of all 4 artifacts into `.capsules/<run>/summary/` and hooking into `run:complete`.\n- **Task `task-summary-cli`**: `orchestrating-long-tasks/scripts/src/cli/commands/summary-ops.ts` implementing `summary:export` and `summary:view`, and routing them in `src/cli/execute.ts`.\n- **Task `task-summary-tests`**: Comprehensive unit tests in `tests/unit/summary/` for timeline, metrics, graph generation, markdown formatter, and CLI export.\n\n#### Group B: `gvui` Repository (`/Users/onurseckinsenoglu/repos/gvui`)\n- **Task `task-gvui-schema`**: Update `gvui/src/types/graphData.ts` to support `sections`, `CommandExecutionDetail`, `FindingDetail`, and rich metadata.\n- **Task `task-gvui-import-script`**: Create `gvui/scripts/import-capsule.ts` and add `\"gvui:import\": \"bun scripts/import-capsule.ts\"` to `gvui/package.json`.\n- **Task `task-gvui-drawer-tabs`**: Enhance the Detail Drawer in `gvui` (`src/components/` & `src/features/`) to provide dedicated tabs for Overview, Files & Diffs, Executed Commands (stdout/stderr), and Validation Findings.\n- **Task `task-gvui-sections`**: Ensure visual group rendering for `GraphSection` in the canvas without touching any layout pathfinding algorithms in `src/engine/`.\n- **Task `task-gvui-tests`**: Unit and integration tests in `gvui` verifying schema validation, capsule import, and drawer tab rendering.\n\n### End-to-End Verification:\n1. Run `bun run typecheck` and `bun test tests/unit` in `skills` -> 100% pass.\n2. Run `bun run typecheck` and `bun test` in `gvui` -> 100% pass.\n3. Export an existing capsule summary (`summary:export`) and import it into `gvui` (`bun run gvui:import`), verifying that the graph dataset loads cleanly in `gvui/public/data/graphs/`.\n4. Seal the run capsule (`critic:start`, `critic:review`, `run:complete`).\n5. Send one concise milestone completion summary to the parent thread when finished.\n"
    },
